ent": "", "type": "text"}]}]}], "stimuli_ids": [], "template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": []}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Activity 3", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!"}, "type": "feedback"}]}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}]}], "type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "The Importance of Javascript", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 6, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 3, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you hear or use to talk about JavaScript.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Understand information about web applications, their principles and basic concepts in a range of work contexts.   Describe applications for an operating system for personal computers in a range of work contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Reads and Writes effective texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context.   Exchanges simple information on web applications, and applications for operating systems for personal computers.", "type": "secondary_1"}]}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob06re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Simple Past Passive", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Remember the <strong>passive voice</strong> focuses on the thing or person that receives the action rather than on the agent that performs it.  ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<b>Simple past passive</b> highlights the thing or person that received an action in the past. If the agent that performed the action is not important, it is possible to omit it. Let's check the following example:<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">I'm sure technology <strong>was implemented</strong> to improve people's quality of life.</span><br/><br/>  The highlight is on \u201ctechnology\u201d and its implementation, not in whoever implemented it.<br/><br/>  The<b> passive voice</b> follows this structure:<br/><br/>  <div class=\"center_text\">Thing or person that receives the action + <b>was/were</b> + <b>past participle</b> + complement</div><br/><br/>   Example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">JavaScript <strong>was adopted</strong> by many companies.</span></br></br> Remember that you can indicate the agent that performed the action by introducing it with the preposition <b>'by'</b> as shown in the previous example. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "JavaScript was created to make programmers' lives easier. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "This widespread tool was so well built that it has been increasing its range of acceptance.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "JavaScript was adopted in our company 5 years ago and since then, it became a \"must\" for programming.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Passive Voice of Modal Verbs, Should, in Affirmative Form", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "The <strong>passive voice</strong> focuses on the thing or person that receives the action rather than on the agent that performs it. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "We can use <strong>passive voice with modal verbs</strong> to show obligation or possibility while emphasizing on the thing or person that is receiving the action. The <b>passive voice </b>follows this structure:<br/><br/>   <div class=\"center_text\">Thing or person that receives the action + <b>modal verb</b> + <b>be</b> + <b>past participle</b> + complement</div><br/><br/>  Examples:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">The advantages of JavaScript <strong>must be taken into account</strong> when determining what programming language to use.<br/> JavaScript <strong>should be implemented</strong> in our company.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "How syntax and operators in programming language work is something that should be studied before starting to write any code. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Contrary to popular belief that software should be constantly updated.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Syntax in programming language is something that should be taken seriously.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "overwhelming ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "causing stress or feeling uncontrollable ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Within the overwhelming world of programming, there is a bunch of things to be taken into account before successfully executing your first JavaScript commands.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob06aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "best suited ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something with the characteristic of fitting perfectly ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We now think it is the best suited technology for us and we are now quite aware of its advantages.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob06aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "widespread ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something that has been shared or commented widely ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This widespread tool was so well built that it has been increasing its range of acceptance, and thus, popularity among users in the past years.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob06aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "a must ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something considered highly necessary or mandatory to do or have  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: JavaScript is a \"must\" for programmers.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob06aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "standpoint", "type": "name"}, {"content": "one's personal opinion or viewpoint ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: From our standpoint, we used to be skeptical about JavaScript since web-based applications were considered an issue in language programming and we thought JavaScript was not going to be any better than the other languages. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob06aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "user-friendly ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something users can easily use  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Overall, its importance relies on all the advantages and user-friendly features it offers.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n6le03ob06aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Search for information related to the importance of JavaScript.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a list of the benefits that JavaScript has brought to modern technology. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Prepare a presentation about these benefits. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your work with the class. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I understand the importance of JavaScript. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I read written information about JavaScript. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write about the relevance of JavaScript. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my work with the class. ", "type": "text"}]}]}